<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n47673" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠχ-έω</span></b> , 
			Aeol.
		and 
			Dor.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀχέω</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc"> [ᾱ</span>]: <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>I.</b> intr., <i>sound, ring, peal</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠχεῖ δὲ κάρη . . Ὀλύμπου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hes.
					<u>Th.</u>
					42
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅταν ἀχήσῃ πολιὸς βυθός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Mosch.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					1.4
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀχοῦσι προσπόλων χέρες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Supp.</u>
					72
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); of metal, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠχέεσκε ὁ χαλκὸς τῆς ἀσπίδος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					4.200
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ χαλκία πληγέντα μακρὸν ἠχεῖ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Prt.</u>
					329a
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Men.
				66.4
			</span></i>; of the grasshopper, <i>chirp</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Alc.
				39
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				16.96
			</span></i>; of the ears, <i>tingle</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠχήσει τὰ ὦτα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					LXX
					<u>1 Ki.</u>
					3.11
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διὰ τί ἠχεῖ ἢ διὰ τί
				ἐμφαίνεται</span>; impers., of <i>anecho</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>AP</u>
				0.98a27
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>suffer from noises in the ears</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Herod.Med.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Orib.
				10.40.3
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> c. acc.
			cogn., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀχεῖν </span>(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰαχεῖν</span> codd.) <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὕμνον</span>
			<i>to let</i> it <i>sound</i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Th.</u>
				869
			</span></i> (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κωκυτόν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Tr.</u>
					866
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γόους</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					523
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὕμνους</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Ion</u>
					883
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χαλκέον ἄχει</span>
			<i>sound</i> the cymbal! <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				2.36
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐφεξῆς ἠχοῦντα αὐτά</span>
			(sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ φωνήεντα</span>) <i><span class="en">
				Demetr.
				<u>Eloc.</u>
				71
			</span></i>: —
				Med.
			, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀχεῖσθαί τινα</span>
			<i>to sound</i> his praises, dub. in <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				75.19
			</span></i>:— 
				Pass.
			, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠχεῖται κτύπος</span> a
			sound <i>is made</i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OC</u>
				1500
			</span></i>. (Cf. sq.)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
